# ENG-1312: a single pre-existing stray NUL byte (predates this file's ENG-1312
# changes — see the "fix: strip a pre-existing stray NUL byte" commit) makes
# git's own content-sniffing heuristic classify this file as binary for ANY
# diff where either side still contains it — which `main` did/does until this
# fix lands there too. `* text=auto` alone does not override that heuristic
# (verified locally: `git diff origin/main HEAD` still rendered "Binary files
# ... differ" with only that rule). The `diff` attribute does — it forces
# git's diff machinery to treat this specific path as text regardless of
# either blob's content, which is what actually makes this PR's diff (and,
# very likely, GitHub's PR view and Greptile's own diff consumption) render
# normally instead of as an opaque binary blob. Safe to remove once `main`
# no longer contains the byte anywhere in this file's history that a PR could
# diff against.
